les":{"year":"2026 so far: 13 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows","records":"Wichita Falls is setting record highs far faster than chance","change":"Wichita Falls' nights cooled over the long run. Its days have warmed since 1986.","rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 63\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>63\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 66\u00b0F, and the record is 85\u00b0F (1955). The low of <strong>43\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Wichita Falls is setting record highs far faster than chance","p_rec":"If Wichita Falls' climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Wichita Falls has set <strong>66 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 95 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">161 record highs</strong>, far more than the 95 that chance alone would give. The 2020s hold the most record highs of any decade (66). Wichita Falls' all-time high is 117\u00b0F, on June 28, 1980.","t_chg":"Wichita Falls' nights cooled over the long run. Its days have warmed since 1986.","p_chg":"Across 102 complete years: Wichita Falls' average low has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.11\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.20 to \u22120.01), about \u22121.1\u00b0F since 1924. Wichita Falls' average high shows no clear change: \u22120.02\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.14 to +0.09) that includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows show no clear change and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.72\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.31 to +1.14). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; April and October fell. Highs rose in none.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Wichita Falls' yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.18 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 27.9 inches a year. The wettest year was 2015 (47.38 in); the driest, 2011 (12.97 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 13 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}